# Known DIFF cases of `cargo xtask abi-diff` for SX-3a's program (abi-ns-mount): "<case>: <owner>: <why>".
# ktest sx.mnt.programs compares V2 with expected/sx3-*.txt (for the errors case: Linux 6.6's answers, see below).
abi-ns-mount errors: desk: Linux 6.6 order, as V2 does; CachyOS 7.3 differs in two lines: umount2(MNT_FORCE) by a user namespace's root is EPERM in 6.6 (linux-6.6/fs/namespace.c:1881 can_umount, capable(CAP_SYS_ADMIN)) and 7.3 unmounts; pivot_root with a bad pointer and no capability is EPERM in 6.6 (may_mount first, namespace.c:4174) and EFAULT in 7.3. Remove when the reference moves past 6.6
abi-ns-mount pty: IN: a pty opened through a devpts instance's ptmx gets its slave in the boot /dev/pts, not in that instance (CR5, Linux devpts_pty_new); "slave in the instance = ENOENT"
